<title>NETHERLANDS: FEDEX DUTCH STRIKE ACTION ENDS.</title>
<headline>FEDEX DUTCH STRIKE ACTION ENDS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strike action has ended at Federal Express in the Netherlands, a FedEx spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;An agreement has been reached between FedEx and the union to the satisfaction of both parties,&quot; he added. No further details were available.</p>
<p>Members of the FNV union, the largest Dutch union, went on strike last Wednesday at several FedEx branches in a dispute over a new salary system that had been introduced.</p>
<p>Union members called off the strike action pending talks. An agreement was finally reached today.</p>
<p>The express operator employs 150 people in the Netherlands.</p>
</text>
